            "«": "←",
            "®": "Δ",
            "»": "→"
          },
          "note": "CDNU line 1. The eight 22-character CDNU lines sit on the bottom eight rows, 7 to 14, one column in so they are centred across (the WCtrlDcsBiosBridge uses rows 3 to 10). The F-14 reports no seat and only the RIO has a CDNU, so every MCDU shows the RIO's CDNU from either seat. The replace map turns the module's stand-ins into the font's glyphs: the font files a double-headed vertical arrow under Δ, a horizontal one under ◀, the scratchpad diamond under □ (it arrives as control code 0x13) and the cursor block under ⬡, because its underscore slot draws a cross."
